<title>BRAZIL: SOY SHIPPING CONDITIONS AT KEY BRAZILIAN PORTS.</title>
<headline>SOY SHIPPING CONDITIONS AT KEY BRAZILIAN PORTS.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Brazilian ports of Paranagua and Santos reported the following conditions for shipping soybeans and soy products:</p>
<p>PARANAGUA:</p>
<p>Vessels: Mariner A loading 54,359 tonnes soybeans. Studzianski loading 27,780 tonnes soybeans/meal. Litrotis loading 54,386 tonnes soymeal. Waiting to dock, seven vessels to load soymeal, one to load soybeans and one for mixed cargo (soybeans/meal).</p>
<p>Road: 261 trucks carrying soybeans arrived on Aug 12, as well as 293 trucks with soymeal and 47 trucks with vegetable oils, including soyoil. Loading: no figures available.</p>
<p>Stocks: no figures available.</p>
<p>SANTOS:</p>
<p>Vessels: Vakhtangov loading 22,000 tonnes soybeans. Waiting to dock, two vessels to load soybeans. At Cutrale terminal, Captain Veniamis loading 22,000 tonnes soymeal. At Cargill private terminal, Orleta Lwowskie loading 57,500 tonnes soymeal. Waiting to dock, one vessel to load 79,700 tonnes</p>
<p>soymeal.</p>
<p>Road: 93 trucks carrying 2,391 tonnes soybeans arrived on Aug 12. Rail: 122 wagons arrived with 7,063 tonnes soybeans as well as six wagons carrying 254 tonnes soymeal.</p>
<p>Loading (Aug 12): 6,529 tonnes soybeans.</p>
<p>Stocks: 24,323 tonnes soybeans, 14,737 tonnes soymeal.</p>
<p>((--Joelle Diderich, Sao Paulo newsroom +55 11 248 5417))</p>
